  <p align="left" class="BodyTextSpaced">If you've been out of the loop (or if you were never in it), <a href="http://www.rpg.net/columns/briefhistory/briefhistory1.phtml" target="_blank">Wizards of the Coast</a> is the company that got rich with a little collectible card game called Magic: The Gathering, then applied some of the prodigious profit from that game to buy original Dungeons &amp; Dragons publisher TSR when the latter was near bankruptcy in 1997.  They remain the largest RPG publisher in the world.</font></p>
  <p><br>
    <br>
